            "op"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        "name": "callisto"
      }
    ],
    "browse": [
      {
        "name": "execute",
        "description": "Run JavaScript that drives the browser: the user's real Chrome-family browser, through the browse extension. The code is an async function body (a single expression is returned; `return` a value to get it back) running in a small sandboxed JavaScript engine on the relay: no Node, no require/import, no fs, process or fetch (fetch belongs to the page: use page.evaluate). Synchronous code stops after about 2 seconds without an await. The result has the returned value (JSON, or the string as is), console output, warnings, and what happened to the page (URL changes, navigations, handoffs, a bot challenge: hand interactive ones to the user with handoff(), never solve or retry-loop them). Return a screenshot (`return await page.screenshot()`) to see it. Tabs are the handle: without `tab`, `page.goto(url)` opens a new tab; the result starts with `tab: <id>`, which you pass as `tab` to the next execute to continue there (with the same `state`). Close tabs you opened when you're done (`page.close()`).",
        "inputSchema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "code": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "JavaScript (an async function body). Globals:\n- page: a Playwright-style Page for the tab passed as `tab`; without one it has no tab until its first goto(url), which opens a new tab. goto(url, {waitUntil, timeout}), url(), title(), content(), evaluate(fn | string, arg), $eval/$$eval, waitForTimeout/Selector/URL/LoadState/Function, click/fill/type/press/hover/selectOption/check/uncheck(selector, ...), locator(selector), getByRole/Text/Label/Placeholder/TestId/AltText/Title, frameLocator, keyboard.press/type, mouse.click/move/wheel, screenshot({path, fullPage}), goBack/goForward/reload, setViewportSize, close(). Locators: click, dblclick, fill, clear, type, pressSequentially, press, hover, check, uncheck, selectOption, setInputFiles, textContent, innerText, innerHTML, inputValue, getAttribute, isVisible/Hidden/Checked/Enabled/Disabled, count, all, first, last, nth, filter, locator, getBy*, waitFor, evaluate, evaluateAll, allTextContents, boundingBox, screenshot, dragTo. Selectors are CSS or Playwright selectors (role=button[name=\"Save\"], text=Sign in, >> nth=0, iframe >> frame >> ...). Locators are strict: one element.\n- context.newPage() (a new tab), context.pages() (the tabs this execute works in and their popups); browser.contexts().\n- snapshot(options?) → a compact outline with refs (options: find, diff, delta, interactive, within, mode: \"aria\"); ref(\"e12\") → a locator for a snapshot ref. Prefer snapshot + ref over guessing selectors.\n- handoff(message, {timeoutMs?, start?}) when only the user can proceed (login, 2FA, captcha, payment); demonstrate(message) to watch the user do a flow.\n- screenshotWithLabels(), screenshotDiff({baseline}), network.start/status/stop/cancel, pageConsole.start/read/stop, webmcp.list/call(name, input).\n- browse.<tool>(args): any browse tool directly (navigate, snapshot, click, fill, type, press, select, hover, drag, scroll, eval, wait_for, dialog, upload, emulate, webmcp, screenshot, screenshot_diff, network, console, recording, tabs, handoff, demonstrate, status, settings); they act in `page`'s tab unless you pass `tab` (browse.navigate without one opens a tab for `page`); returns its JSON and throws its error.\n- files.path(name), files.write(name, data), files.read(name, encoding?) inside the file roots (files.dir, files.roots).\n- state: an object kept with the tab between execute calls that pass it as `tab` (JSON values only).\n- console.log/warn/error (shown in the result), setTimeout/clearTimeout/setInterval/clearInterval."
            },
            "timeoutMs": {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 0,
              "description": "Overall timeout in milliseconds (paused while handoff waits on the user); default 60000, 0 for none. Includes waiting behind another execute in the same tab."
            },
            "tab": {
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "string"
              ],
              "description": "The tab `page` stands for: the `tab` an earlier execute (or navigate, tabs) returned, or a chosen id like `work-mail` given to tabs new. Leave it out to start without a tab; page.goto(url) then opens one."
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "code"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false
        }
      }
    ]
  },
